WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.420
- I'm happy to call him a friend,

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:03.920
Christian Siriano y'all, how you doing?

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.006
- Let me tell ya, huh, it's tough.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.143
(laughing)
But, doing good, doing good.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.100
- But the world has changed a bit,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.700
since we last saw each other.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.450
So how are you staying
sane in all of this?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.940
- Yeah, I know, it's
been wild, it really has.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.280
I mean, I live in New York,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.783
which has really got hit pretty hard.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.900
And it's a weird place,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.883
to see everything closed
and it's kind of wild.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.430
But I've been listening to the
governor kind of every day,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.590
and there was such a shortage of things

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.010
and I was like, "Well,
maybe I can do something."

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.380
So that's kind of like why I
started just kinda pitching in.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.083
I felt like maybe we could help.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.900
And that was kind of it.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.960
I just felt I couldn't sit
at home and do nothing.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.460
- It's so devastating.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.920
Like you're in a very devastating area

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.250
with this whole virus.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.580
You know, it's really cool though.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.110
I just wanted to say thank you

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.040
because you could just be
chillin' and doing nothing.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:01.873
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:01.873 --> 00:01:02.740
You could just be relaxing

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:03.867
and a lot of people are just like,

00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:05.600
"Okay, I'm just gonna
stay safe and healthy."

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.640
And you heard a need for something,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.800
and then used your talent
for this and it's super cool.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.300
And I just wanted to say thank you

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.800
for doing that, for something.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.120
Everybody doing something matters.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.740
So what is the process
though, of making masks

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.186
'cause that's very different
from dresses and outfits?

00:01:22.186 --> 00:01:23.270
(both laugh)
So I'm like,

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.992
yes, is that hard or is it weird?

00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:26.900
- Its wild, it's like wild.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.100
I mean I literally,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.920
after I tweeted at the
governor and they responded,

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.120
they gave us kinda permission

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.430
to open my office with a small team.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.480
And I realized my sewers
are like couture sewers

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.990
and now they're making masks.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.780
It's quite monotonous work.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.690
It's the same thing over and over again

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:45.340
and at the beginning we
were only making like white

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.520
and now I was like we
need to have some color.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.270
I need something because we've
done like almost 15,000 masks

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.410
and you're like,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.243
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.
- oh my gosh,

00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:57.120
your eyes are bulging out
'cause it's the same thing.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.310
And it's kind of hard,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.730
to make quality control when you,

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.360
I didn't have a mask factory

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.580
and I just kinda turned it into one.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.230
So it's kinda wild.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.580
- Yeah, because there are like,

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.970
I guess specifications in what the mask

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.560
has to be able to do and the filtration.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.550
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.930
We've looked at it too 'cause I quilt

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.160
and I've thought of doing
it with my five-year-old

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.220
on our little sewing machine here

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.387
just trying to make stuff and I was like,

00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:22.880
"Oh gosh, I gotta figure
out all how to do that."

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.810
I was like, it's so crazy--

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.313
- You gotta thread the
machine and it's really hard.

